            <ArticleTitle>Patient safety in interventional pain procedures.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>423-32</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.pmr.2012.02.014</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The objective of this article was to present a systematic review of the safety issues encountered in interventional pain management. Patient safety is an important consideration in the practice of interventional pain management. Although there is a paucity of scientific articles addressing this topic, the authors have reviewed the literature and present a review of the topic, as well as strategies to minimize the risk to patients undergoing interventional spine procedures.</AbstractText>
